appears in EACH of MATERIALIZER_PATHS and OBS_PATHS) so single-manifest removal genuinely fails, since the derive-and-diff union gate cannot detect it.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["check_deploy_manifest.py:80-102 parse_manifest_paths matches every `^[A-Z_]+_PATHS=` line and returns their UNION of tokens","check_deploy_manifest.py:105-111 is_covered() / :207-215 uncovered() test membership against that single merged token set — not any specific manifest","AC4: 'removing a cap script from a consuming manifest makes the deploy-manifest checker fail'","ACs 1&2 require the SAME scripts in BOTH MATERIALIZER_PATHS and OBS_PATHS, so single-manifest removal is masked by the union","Existing tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py:83-98 only proves the total-removal case (re.sub removes ALL occurrences)"],"finding":"AC4 ('removing a cap script from a consuming manifest makes the deploy-manifest checker fail') cannot be satisfied by the reused derive-and-diff checker, which tests coverage against the UNION of all *_PATHS. Because ACs 1 & 2 require each cap script in BOTH MATERIALIZER_PATHS and OBS_PATHS, removing it from only one manifest leaves it in the union, so is_covered() stays True and the gate stays green — the regression test can only fail on total removal from every manifest, not from 'a consuming manifest'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa28f6784bae41dcf","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC4), and its interaction with ACs 1-3 / scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py","norm_id":"nbe9585a7d4982303","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit drops docker-storage-cap.sh from MATERIALIZER_PATHS but leaves it in OBS_PATHS: compose-up.sh --install re-materialization signal is lost, yet the deploy-manifest gate passes green because the union still covers it.","The AC4 regression test is written to remove a cap from one 'consuming manifest' and assert failure — it cannot go RED against the union-only checker, so the test is either impossible-as-worded or gives false assurance."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Keep the derive-and-diff gate for union coverage (AC3), but add an explicit per-manifest test that parses MATERIALIZER_PATHS and OBS_PATHS individually and asserts every derived `infra/**/*-cap.sh` path is present in BOTH — this is the only mechanism that makes AC4's 'a consuming manifest' clause non-vacuous, and it matches the plan's two-independent-consumers rationale.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"4fbb8acd11bf5617","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["1b1b0c323e4aa6ad",2039],"description_boxes":["399141be1d30ac26",0],"file_impact":["5fc03923170513b7",3],"ticket_id":["2ff843e303cebf6e",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":584398,"cache_write_tokens":187889,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms